{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"ruin_column","model_identifier":"ruin_column","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# ruin_column\n\nViolet ruin, part 2: a wide column of violet light (radius about 330 u, 640 u = 18 m tall, a translucent shell of tangent light panels round a solid white-violet core) that slams down into the `ruin_warning` ring.\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -360..358, y 0..640, z -359..359 units (20.19 x 18.00 x 20.20 m). Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 256 x 1024, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering; every visible face has its own region painted with its material at world position (identical faces share one). No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: 88.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 718 x 640 x 718 (w x h x d), centred at x -1, z 0\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | what moves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `slam` | 0.5 | once | the column drops from the sky (from y +640) and hits the ground at 0.25 s, then holds |\n\n- Glowing cubes (`glow_*`): glow_col_core0, glow_col_core1, glow_col_outer0, glow_col_outer1, glow_col_outer10, glow_col_outer11, glow_col_outer12, glow_col_outer13, glow_col_outer14, glow_col_outer15, glow_col_outer16, glow_col_outer17 ...\n\n## Notes\n\n- Bright simple glowing shapes; every lit cube is named `glow_*` (flat colours; the game may scale, spin and fade them). No particles or lights in the file.\n- Built from 33 identical tangent panels (one shared 1 px/unit texture region), a core of two crossed boxes and two impact rings, so every face keeps square pixels with no stretching. The outer shell uses a texture with alpha (about 47 %); the core is solid white-violet.\n"},"resolution":{"width":256,"height":1024},"elements":[{"name":"glow_col_outer0","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission":0,"render_order":"default","allow_mirr